            <ArticleTitle>Quantitative relation between the intensity of tooth pulp stimulation and the magnitude of jaw opening reflex in the rat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1173-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The stimulus-response relation in the jaw opening reflex evoked by tooth pulp stimulation, which is considered as a &quot;pain index&quot;, follows the power function with an exponent of about six over a range of lower stimulus intensities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
